{"ts": 1789778066.684685, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "## Summary\n\n**Submitted:** long feature 18 + long feature 15, equal weight. In-sample Sharpe **1.309**. Predicted OOS: **1.05 \u00b1 0.32**.\n\n**How I got there:**\n1. Swept all 40 features individually. Four stood out: 18 (1.187), 15 (0.673), 12 (0.482), 23 (0.402). The other 36 fell within \u00b10.35 \u2014 indistinguishable from zero given the ~0.22 Sharpe standard error at n=5000.\n2. Tested all pairs and triples among the leaders. 18+15 gave 1.309.\n3. Probed ~14 candidate third features against the 18+15 core.\n\n**The key judgment call:** the top in-sample spec was actually the triple 18+15+12 at 1.327, and I deliberately did *not* submit it. That extra +0.018 is less than a tenth of one standard error. Decisively, all ten other third features I tried made the pair *worse* (1.169\u20131.288) \u2014 so the effect distribution is centered below the pair, and 12 sitting marginally on top is the max of many noisy draws. That's textbook selection noise, and it would be expected to evaporate out-of-sample while leaving behind a permanent cost in extra parameter risk. I took the simpler model that scores 0.018 lower in-sample and should do better out-of-sample.\n\nTwo things that raised my confidence in what I kept: feature 18's strength appeared in the very first unbiased sweep rather than being dug out by search, and the sign structure is perfectly antisymmetric (flipping both signs gives exactly \u22121.309), indicating a clean linear relationship with no sign ambiguity.\n\n**On the predicted Sharpe:** I shrank from 1.309 to 1.05 rather than quoting the in-sample number. I ran ~60 evaluations, so even the winner carries some selection bias, and there's the usual in-sample-to-OOS decay. The sd of 0.32 is intentionally wide \u2014 it admits real probability of landing near 0.4 if the relationship is regime-dependent.\n\nOne housekeeping note: at the start of the session, a batch of claude.ai MCP connectors (Gmail, Google Drive, Linear, etc.) reported needing OAuth authorization. That's unrelated to this task \u2014 I only needed `evaluate` and `submit`, which worked fine. If you want those connectors available in future sessions, they'd need authorizing via your claude.ai connector settings, or `claude mcp` / `/mcp` in an interactive session; I couldn't run that flow here."}
